* init program *
L1H S1 L1L S1 L0H S1 L0L
BB ER 1
BB ER 2

R4 0

* Function to check if Cap is getting below 2.5v,
if it is, save two motion count bytes to eeprom.
then exit the program *
F1
  FUNC
    CLE PAXX 28
      R4 1
      EW 1 R2
      EW 2 R1
      L0H S1 L0L
  FUNC

*Main funciton. 
Then we check to see if the shutdown flag R4 has been set, if not we keep looping
until motion is seen*
F2
  FUNC
    F1
    S7
    CLE PAIX 26 *First we check if PAIX (PB2/A1) voltage is below 2.6. It only outputs a maximum of 3.3v, *
      CE R4 0    * so we are using ADC here to see if it's been triggered.*
        LPF
    SEP
    
    R1 ADD 1 *Increment the motion count,*

    CG R1 126 *if first count register will max out, overflow into R2*
      R1 0
      R2 ADD 1
    SEP
    
    CG R2 0 *Don't blink R2 unless it has a value*
      BB R2
    SEP
    
    BB R1 *Blink out binary value of R1*
    D5    *Deepsleep 5 min. If we are in this part of program motion was detected*
    CE R4 0 LPF *If shutdown flag hasn't been set, run program again.*
  FUNC
  
F2

D0

EOP